# Applies to this directory only, which is Scaling/ inside the drawing-quality
# clone. Nothing outside it is affected, so the rest of the repository keeps its
# own rules.
#
# Tracked, and why:
#
#   contexts/**        the contexts, the scales derived from them, their
#                      manifests, nesting matrices, groupings and READMEs. These
#                      are inputs, not outputs: a scale encodes a judgement about
#                      which distinctions matter and cannot be regenerated from
#                      anything but its groupings file.
#   Datasets/**        the raw material the contexts are built from.
#   *.py, tests/**     the code, including the small .cxt files the regression
#                      tests pin.
#   *.csv              the results: scales, drawings, consistency, strata,
#                      sensitivity.
#   graphml/           the drawings themselves. Regenerable in principle, but
#                      hours of compute: freese alone takes 464 s at 319 concepts.
#   drawings/          their PDF renders.
#   figures/           the gate figures.
#   pipeline.md        how the pipeline works and what it found.
#   README.md          layout and setup.
#
# Ignored: the local environment, the separately cloned paper repository, run
# logs, the private working notes, and the reference papers.

# A separate clone with its own remote. Never commit it into this one.
paper/

# Private working notes, not part of the shared repository.
CLAUDE.md
TODO.md
HANDOVER.md
writing/

# Local Python environment. Recreate it from requirements.txt instead.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Run logs and scratch directories.
logs/
*.log
.profile-scratch/
.dimdraw-sensitivity/
.mapping-check.json
# dim-flux writes this into the working directory and removes it again.
input.cxt

# Reference papers kept locally for reading; not ours to redistribute. Only at
# this level, so figures/*.pdf still tracks.
/*.pdf

# SSH public key left in the working directory.
key.pub

# LaTeX build products
*.aux
*.out
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.brf
*.lbl
